    "done_when": "§7's reference-loader paragraph is the specification. imas_ambix/eval/efit_referee.py gains one loader with the seam's signature, (shot_id, frame_times, **kwargs) -> EquilibriumGeometry, passed as read_efit_geometry(..., loader=...). It is not exported in __all__ and adds no public name. It reads the shot's record through imas_ambix/data/selene_psrc.py read_psrc_record, forwarding cache_root and extractor from its kwargs. It reduces the record through imas_ambix/worldmodel/equilibrium_labels.py build_geometry_from_arrays and re-derives nothing. t_eq is the boundary's time base. The magnetic axis (calRp0, calZp0) and the X-point (calRX, calZX) are interpolated onto t_eq, and the X-point is passed as a one-null set with time on the last axis. The boundary's per-slice contours are passed with time on the last axis, in a form the builder's per-slice LCFS resampling accepts even when slices hold different vertex counts. Read resample_lcfs_radii and handle NaN padding explicitly rather than assume it. PSRC's geometric centre calCCSRc/calCCSZc is never read. The read happens only inside evaluator_context: called outside it, read_efit_geometry raises FirewallViolation as for every loader. The static import guard in tests/eval/test_efit_referee.py, which asserts that no world-model or training source references efit_referee, also asserts that none references imas_ambix.data.selene_psrc. New tests in tests/eval/test_selene_reference.py use a tmp_path cache seeded read-only from /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/100599.zarr PSRC (calRX, calZX, calRp0, calZp0, calIp, and calCCSRc and calCCSZc for the control, with their time bases), plus a synthetic surfABVxp in mm with two slices of different vertex counts. They show four things: the loader's axis equals calRp0 and calZp0 interpolated at a frame time; both slices resample to finite LCFS radii; a call outside evaluator_context raises FirewallViolation; and judge_geometry scores a model geometry equal to the loader's output at zero boundary RMS. No test opens ssh, and nothing under /work is written. Write a landing fragment docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-selene-reference-loader.html. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), run in the foreground and capture once, to a log in the run directory whose first lines give the committed revision the tests ran at and the full command with its PYTHONPATH, and whose last line is EXIT=: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/eval/test_selene_reference.py tests/eval/test_efit_referee.py; it exits 0, and uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
